FROM THE GM'S DESK
------------------
Spring flushing wrapped up two days early this year - nice work to the field
crew. Our 2025 Water Quality Report goes to the Board in May and will be on
the website by the end of June. The FY26 mid-year budget amendment passed in
April; see the Board minutes on the Public drive for details.   - Greg L.

INTAKE PS-1 PUMP 3 IS BACK
--------------------------
After a 9-week rebuild, Pump P-103 at the Cedar River Intake is back in
service as the standby unit. Miguel Santos and Curtis Webb replaced the
impeller and wear rings and recalibrated the vibration transmitters. Marcus
Oyelaran updated the PLC logic so P-103 rotates into lead duty monthly.
Reminder: P-101 and P-102 are in AUTO; please do not put any intake pump in
HAND without calling the control room (x4220) first.

SUMMIT TANK MIXING PROJECT
--------------------------
Engineering (Walter Pruitt, Hannah Cole) has selected a passive inlet
mixing system for the Summit Elevated Tank to bring down water age and the
summer TTHM peaks we saw in 2025. Install is planned for October, which
means the tank comes out of service for about 10 days and Hilltop PS-3 will
run in direct-pump mode. Expect overtime sign-ups from Operations.

